t up with a  local guy who grew up here who's a Game  of Thrones fan and when we were out and  about talking about the show he  mentioned that he had the exact same  experience he had heard the show had  dragons and wasn't interested so the  moral of the story is that the relative  on coolness of flying magical beasts  crosses multiple cultures now obviously  I've evolved on the subject  after all I'm making my second  dragon-related video in as many days I  started watching the show realized it  was a good story and eventually became  hooked as soon as Ned lost his head in  the beginning when I told people about  the show I actually even say things like  it has some magic and stuff but it  doesn't take away from the show here's  the thing though dragons in general may  be the things of children's stories they  may even be the spirit animal of the  biggest weirdo you've ever met but take  a step back and think about the role  they play in this completely made-up  world we all casually talked about in  the comments like it's real besides the  men and everything else that inhabits  this world one of the forces of nature  that shaped it are the Dragons the  Valyrian freehold is the mightiest  Empire Empire that planet OSes that  likely ever known they were far more  technologically advanced than their  neighbors and basically held on to their  power through their dragons now despite  being so advanced they weren't the  greatest people they had the super  weapon and they used it to enslave other  civilizations to the dirty to do their  dirty work of mining for them eventually  the doom came and wiped them all out  except for one Dragon Lord family who  got the idea from a dream the close up  shop and clip moved closer to Westeros  this of course was the Targaryen family  who used their dragons to conquer the  entirety of their new home it didn't  happen overnight but they used their  super weapon to roll over all the long  existing kingdoms that made up Westeros  so you see what the Dragons are their  weapons and their effective ones that  there isn't a great counter for like  think about Cersei super weapon the  mountain not much use against a dragon  or three in fact that Targaryen only had  problems when they started fighting  against each other their Dragons didn't  die off until the dance and they didn't  lose the iron throne until about 150  years after they lost their dragons  would there have been a successful  rebellion if they still had them  probably not anyways in my war for the  dawn video I laid out my thinking in  relation to another supernatural force  in this world that's advancing towards  humanity the White Walkers who raised  the dead to fight for them are headed in  man's direction and by man  mankind they haven't done anything like  this for about eight thousand years and  back then it was pretty devastating to  put it into perspective on how a special  weapon might be needed just think about  brands direwolf summer bravely summer  sacrificed himself to slow the weights  down and it didn't work at all like he  didn't even hold them up or buy them  five extra seconds so if you're really  hoping to see john fighting alongside  goes taking out the white walkers one by  one be careful what you wish for the  dragons on the other hand are weapons of  mass destruction and one that our pals  are going to need before the series ends  if it's any consolation at least the  breaker of chains and the guy who only  ever wanted to be accepted into the  family he that raised him are the ones  who are closest to this powerful weapon  right now I mean it could be worse what  if little finger had dragons or Europe  that's not how the story is set up  though and that's why Game of Thrones  dragons are actually cool and not cheesy  at all in the past people who used them  as a weapon for personal gain or to  suppress other people eventually felt  here they actually serve a purpose and  in that sense they make the story better  when you look at the big picture so I'm  not saying that the you know the world  for the dawn or and you know nothing  surprising is gonna happen there but  it's going to happen and whether the  Dragons open the door for a diplomatic  solution or they're just a powerful  weapon that destroys the White Walkers  one way or another they're essential to  even the score the other thing I wanted  to address in this video is a question  comment I got over and over again it's  the idea that bran will use his warding  abilities to skin change one of the  remaining dragons thus becoming like the  third head of the Dragon comes from the  idea that the three-eyed Raven told him  that he wouldn't be able to walk again  but he would fly I've never been a fan  of this theory for several reasons and  so I'm biased about it for sure it's not  outside the realm of possibilities but  there are a lot of strong arguments  against it personally I believe that  when the Bloodraven said that what he  was that bran would be able to leave  where he was under the tree and fly by  looking through the weirwoods of course  he can also skin change ravens and stuff  like that but I don't think that's what  he meant  the simplest example I can think of to  explain why is that he says you won't  walk when Brandt enters summer or Hodor  he does actually walk so even though he  can fly through Ravens it just doesn't  make sense that this was the meaning  behind what he said for me this means he  didn't say it to give us a clue that  Brandi would eventually take over one of  the Dragons I could be wrong here and I  wouldn't be totally upset if the story  works but that's just how I feel about  it there's also the whole vert Muir  story in the costuming from his mentor  Hagin about taking over people when Vera  Muir tries to do it it doesn't end well  which makes me believe something similar  would probably happen with a dragon plus  on top of that there's no history of a  person ever skin changing a dragon that  in any of the stories as far as that  third dragon is concerned that's another  video altogether like dragon video  number five from a person that was  skeptical about ever starting to watch  the show because they were involved in  the first place anyways that's what I  think about the brand we'll work a  dragon theory flame away in the comments  if you like but also leave a comment if  you agree please like the video if you  enjoyed it and don't forget to subscribe  to become eligible for the new giveaway  also follow me on my social media  accounts you can find the links in the  video description or on my channel page  and I'm always on Twitter when I'm not  on YouTube about the giveaway when I hit  28,000 subscribers I will get one lucky  commenting fan a copy of the great  looking 20th anniversary edition of Game  of Thrones all you have to do to enter  is be a subscriber and comment on any or  all of the videos where I mentioned the  giveaway for more info on how it works  you can check out my Dragonstone video  to see how the winner was selected in  the first giveaway thanks for watching  I'll talk to you soon
 

